# Dredge: "A player with fewer cards in their library than the number required by a dredge ability can't mill any of them this
# way" (CR 702.52b) - "you can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library" (its ruling).
# Bot1's library holds five cards when its turn 3 draw comes, and Golgari Grave-Troll's is dredge 6: Bot1 is not asked, and
# draws as usual. (The scenario beside this one, with six or more, asks.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Thoughtseize
Golgari Grave-Troll
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Forest x5

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thoughtseize.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Choose(Golgari Grave-Troll)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 5
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains; Forest
Bot1.Graveyard = Thoughtseize; Golgari Grave-Troll
Bot1.Library.Count = 4
